      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my realtor just mentioned i need to set up an escrow account for the house i'm buying in toronto. i've never heard of that before... what exactly is escrow and why do i need it for the closing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow, in the context of real estate, is a trust account that holds funds for various expenses related to the property purchase. It's a common practice in many countries, including Canada, where your realtor is likely familiar with it. Think of it like a temporary home for your funds, where they're safely kept until the closing date, when the funds are disbursed for the various costs associated with the transaction.\n\nYou need an escrow account for the closing because it ensures that the seller receives the funds for the property, and you receive the ownership of the property, all at the same time. It's like a little insurance policy, where the funds are held until the deal is finalized, and then released in a controlled manner. You don't want to be like a poor goblin who's just discovered a treasure trove of gold coins, only to have them stolen by a sneaky thief – you want to ensure that the transaction is smooth and secure.\n\nIn Toronto, the escrow account typically holds funds for the following expenses: the purchase price of the property, property taxes, and any other costs associated with the transaction. The funds are usually disbursed on the closing date, when the transaction is complete. Your realtor will guide",
