      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I just couldn't help myself, I guess I was thinking of a certain goblin who was known for his love of gold coins. Anyway, back to the escrow account.\n\nIn Canada, the escrow account is typically managed by a third-party escrow agent, such as a lawyer, a real estate agent, or a specialized escrow company. These agents are usually licensed and regulated by the relevant authorities, so you can trust that they'll handle the funds responsibly.\n\nThink of an escrow agent like a guardian of the treasure, keeping the funds safe and secure until the transaction is complete. They're like a protective shield, guarding against any potential risks or disputes that might arise during the transaction.\n\nIn Toronto, the escrow agent is usually a lawyer or a real estate agent who's experienced in handling escrow accounts. They'll work closely with your realtor and the seller's agent to ensure that the funds are disbursed correctly and on time.\n\nAs for the safety of the funds, don't worry – the escrow agent has a fiduciary duty to hold the funds in trust, which means they're legally obligated to keep the funds separate from their own assets and to return the funds to you when the transaction is complete. It",
